WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 5: Actions and Activities.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.940
You will learn thirteen action words,
including build, discuss, protect and celebrate.

3
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:15.640
You will talk about what you did using the past
simple, explain reasons and results with because and so,

4
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:22.740
order events with First, Next, Then and Finally,
ask Wh- questions, and share opinions politely.

5
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:31.480
The unit story, “The Wall Behind the Garden”, follows Amal,
Leo and their class as they build a reading wall together.

6
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:37.400
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:44.300
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
and use many action words, such as build, listen,

8
00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:45.700
protect and celebrate.

9
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:52.000
You will also talk about things you did, using
the past simple (built, listened, celebrated).

10
00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:57.040
You will also explain why something
happened, using because and so.

11
00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.760
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

12
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.800
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: care, dare, bear, pear, pair, check.

13
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:11.020
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

14
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.180
The reading sequence includes A
Busy Saturday and Helping Hands.

15
00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:20.120
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

16
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.320
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

17
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.740
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

18
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.760
We use the past simple to talk about actions
that already happened and are finished.

19
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.680
It helps us tell stories and share the things we did.

20
00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:42.260
In this unit's story the children built
a wall, so we say built, not build.

21
00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.820
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

22
00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.300
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — Tell What You Did.

23
00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.340
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

24
00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:00.800
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

25
00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.720
You are ready to begin.

26
00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:08.480
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

27
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:15.620
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
